  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe propose a principled optimization strategy using convex relaxation and iterative improvement to achieve a tighter upper bound. The key challenges we address are:\n1. Complex nonconvex optimization landscape\n2. Need to efficiently explore the discrete nature of step functions\n3. Maintaining feasibility (0<=h\u22641, \u222bh=1) at all steps\n\nOur approach combines:\n- A well-defined mathematical program with smoothed analysis\n- Iterative constructive methods with convex separation\n- Robust feasibility maintenance through scaled projections\n\nThe central idea is to represent the optimization problem as:\nMinimize max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\nsubject to 0\u2264h\u22641, \u222bh=1\n\nWe use a novel formulation that utilizes Hadamard transforms and integral constraints. This method ensures:\n- Linear separation among candidate solutions\n- Progressive refinement through gradient sweeping\n- Noise-free gradient computation via analytical methods\n\nThe approach is both theoretically sound and computationally feasible. We estimate that this method can achieve improved bounds due to its structured exploration and systematic refinement.\n\nMathematical specification:\nWe represent h as a vector spaces with:\n- Dimension n_points (default 280)\n- Integral constraint favorable to gradient-based search\n- Analytical gradient computation using correlation transforms\n\nThe objective is defined as:\nC_max = (dx) * max_k | \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx |\nwhere dx=2/n_points\n\nThe mathematical program uses:\n- Equality constraint: sum(h) * dx = 1\n- Box constraints: 0\u2264h[i]\u22641\n- Finite differencing guardrails\n\nImplementation procedure:\n\n1. Problem representation:\n   - Accept seed (42), budget (1100s), **kwargs\n   - Set up parameter space with n_sweep = 1500\n   - Initialize h0 from initial_h_values if available\n\n2. Convex-reformulation engine:\n   a) Projection onto feasible set: While not feasible, project until constraints meet\n   b) Gradient computation via Fourier transforms\n   c) Trust-region update with adaptive radius\n\n3. Iterative refinement:\n   Correlation mode analysis with:\n      - Low-frequency filtering\n      - Multiscale gradient application\n      - Regularization strength sweep [0.1, 10]\n      - Direction selection from eigenvalue decomposition\n\n4. Candidate selection:\n   a) Initialize with steps [0,1] with integral = 1\n   b) Main loop (n_points_stages=15 iterations):\n      i) Compute correlation profile and identify critical lags\n      ii) Perform active-set projection for worst lags\n      iii) Update feasibility via scaled projection\n      iv) Adjust regularization parameter\n      v) Push toward target bound through gradient communication\n\n5. Feasibility maintenance:\n   Use quadrilateral projection method ensuring:\n      - Integral constraint is strictly maintained\n      - Box constraints are satisfied\n      - No dimension reduction\n\n6. Termination conditions:\n   - Exceeded timer: min(c, budget)\n   - Stability criteria: gradient norm < 1e-6\n   - Max iterations reached\n\nSearch choices:\n\n- Primary dimension n_sweep = 1500\n- Lag selection: top 5 dynamic based on correlation\n- Regularization: adaptive sweep with centering\n- Stability triggers: tolerance, iteration limit\n\nComputebudget and robustness:\n\n- Major cost: matrix transforms (O(n^2 log n))\n- Time estimates: n=280: ~240s (without fallback), ~840s with fallback\n- Slicing based on n_points:\n   n_points=280: phase1=400s, phase2=300s, polishing=300s\n   n_points=560: 1600s (sliced by factors of 2)\n\nValidation and return contract:\n\n- Precompute grid positions [0,2/n_points,...,2]\n- Check integral: within 1e-6 of 1\n- Check box constraints: 0<=h[i]<=1 for all i\n- Final correlation: precise float output\n- Residual handling: clip to 0.3800 floor if under target\n\nThe entire process is designed to achieve a convex envelope over the full optimization landscape, combining guaranteed feasibility with noise-free gradient exploration to systematically approach the theoretical minimum.",
